  "body": "Found in the review of PR #3229 (#3206), comment 7068630733.\n\nIn the wire-EDM ISO post (`script_wire_iso`), the U word (about line 375) and the taper angle (about line 357) are not checked for a finite value. A non-finite value then posts as `UNaN` or `ANaN` in the program. The X, Y, I and J words go through the checked path.\n\nWrong posted G-code is P1 in the AGENTS.md table: the post must refuse the program by name, never write a word that no control can read.\n\nWork:\n1. Check U, V and the taper angle for a finite value before they are written, as the other words are checked.\n2. Refuse the program by name when a value is not finite.\n3. Add a pinning test: a non-finite U and a non-finite taper angle are refused, and no NC file is written.\n",
